WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.417
RAG becomes much easier to understand when we separate indexing time from question time.

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:10.107
Indexing happens before a user asks anything.

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:15.312
We load documents, clean them, create chunks, generate embeddings, and store vectors with metadata.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:24.302
For a stable knowledge base, this work may happen once and then run again only when documents change.

00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:25.242
Question time begins when a user sends a query.

00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:32.152
We embed that question, retrieve the best chunks, build a prompt using those chunks,

00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:34.477
and ask the language model to generate an answer.

00:00:34.477 --> 00:00:40.902
[tts-break] This separation is important for both performance and debugging.

00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:48.497
If retrieval is slow, you need to know whether the problem is in indexing or query-time search.

00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:54.642
If an answer is stale, you may need to inspect the indexing pipeline rather than the language model.

00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:59.917
Keep these two flows in mind throughout the module: prepare knowledge first,

00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:02.960
then use that prepared knowledge to answer questions.
